# Game over's end, back to the SEGA screen (build 157a). GameOverScreen
# returns on B or C, or after $708 frames, with game_screen already
# ScreenID_Sega (the battle set it, loc_F266); MainGameLoop runs
# SegaScreen, which sends $E0 -- the music fades -- and darkens the
# message and its picture (PaletteFadeFrom, red first) before its setup.
# Until 157a the port cut straight to the logo's setup. A level-1 Rolf
# against Mother Brain loses in a round (gameover_message's way in).

start battle $103
party 1 1
limit 4000
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen gameover
# (build 157c) GameOverScreen's erase takes the battle's windows with the
# rest: plane A cells, their tiles among 0-$5BF. Until 157c the port
# reset the window system as the screen began, and they went at once.
wait ticks 16
shot 00_erasing
expect pixel 20 177 $800     # the party window's fill, half its places
wait ticks 384
shot 01_game_over
expect pixel 80 89 $EEE
press c
wait ticks 2
# Three steps in, the message's white has lost three of its red; four
# more and the red is gone (PaletteDecreaseColor: red, then green, then
# blue, one level an entry a step). On 157 the frame was black here.
shot 02_fading
expect pixel 80 89 $EE8
wait ticks 4
shot 03_fading
expect pixel 80 89 $EE0
wait screen sega
shot 04_sega
